<h2 id="ha-ctrl-011-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Exercise no target, no records, Recorder exclusion, purged history and a request failure separately. Never fabricate zeroes.
2. Change targets and periods rapidly; compare heading, plot, table and export scope. Delayed responses must not overwrite a newer selection.
3. Compare raw state history with a supported statistic for the same period and label their different meaning. Preserve signs, gaps and original units.
4. Test native keyboard zoom/source selection and actual download contents. Log any inaccessible value route as an unresolved native issue; a static documentation table is not live verification.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

